-- title:
--   Units of the conjugated order B∩βwidehatΛβ⁻¹
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and write $B=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ for the associated quaternion algebra, and let $\widehat{B}=B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring `FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ`. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $B$ which is an order in the sense of the project's predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $B$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $\beta\in\widehat{B}^{\times}$ and $u\in B$. Write $\widehat{\Lambda}$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14), the additive subgroup of $\widehat{B}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele that is integral at every height-one prime of $\mathbb{Z}$. Then $u$ is a unit of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele Λ β`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31), that is, $u$ lies in the preimage of $\beta\widehat{\Lambda}\beta^{-1}$ under $x\mapsto x\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}1$ and has a two-sided multiplicative inverse lying in that same preimage, if and only if there is a unit $\mu\in\widehat{B}^{\times}$ stabilising the set $\widehat{\Lambda}$ under the pointwise multiplication action of units (the subgroup [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26)) with $u\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}1=\beta\mu\beta^{-1}$ in $\widehat{B}$.
--
--   This is the unit specification for a conjugated order: the unit group of $\Lambda^{\beta}=B\cap\beta\widehat{\Lambda}\beta^{-1}$ is exactly $B\cap\beta\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}\beta^{-1}$, with $\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}$ realised as the stabiliser of $\widehat{\Lambda}$ in $\widehat{B}^{\times}$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where degeneracy data on class sets are built and the associated fibre counts must be shown to depend only on double cosets.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_isUnitOf_conjByFiniteIdele_iff.lean

